    {
      "name": "one-ticking-callback",
      "status": "pass",
      "detail": [
        [
          "C-TICK",
          "`_physics_process(delta)` on the active Encounter coordinator only",
          "Encounter",
          "Complete phases P0\u2013P6 once when initialized, current, unpaused and outside a held transition. Reject reentry and retired/unready invocations. Only successful P6 increments the tick. Helpers run synchronously inside this invocation and cannot schedule another step."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "default-deny-callback-coverage",
      "status": "pass",
      "detail": [
        "F-ASYNC",
        "F-CONTROL",
        "F-INPUT",
        "F-LIFECYCLE",
        "F-OTHER",
        "F-PHYSICS",
        "F-PROCESS",
        "F-SIGNAL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ordered-phases",
      "status": "pass",
      "detail": [
        [
          "P0: eligibility",
          "Encounter, C-TICK guard",
          "Check current initialized encounter, unpaused state, no retirement/held error and no reentry. Finish any required non-advancing cancel drain before sampling actions. A rejected invocation does not consume an input frame or increment the tick."
        ],
        [
          "P1: command boundary",
          "Encounter `submit_action` / InputAdapter `read_frame`",
          "Capture one immutable command batch and input frame for this tick. Validate encounter/input generation, command identity and current permissions. Reject stale/duplicate/invalid requests; later arrivals wait for a later boundary. Consume each physical edge at most once."
        ],
        [
          "P2: rules and intent",
          "Encounter composed controllers",
          "Evaluate current actions and due time-dependent rules using the same `h` and admitted definitions. Derive movement/action intents and staged timer changes in documented stable order. No actor callback supplies another delta. Product admission policies remain with their question/producer cards."
        ],
        [
          "P3: movement and synchronization",
          "Encounter requests CollisionQueries `resolve_movement` / `interpret_contacts`",
          "Start from the last committed authoritative poses and one identified collision-world revision. Resolve movers in stable entity-ID order; later movers see prior resolved physical updates in that order. CollisionQueries completes and identifies the post-movement query world before any attack query. Encounter stages the returned gameplay poses and contact consequences."
        ],
        [
          "P4: attack commitments",
          "Encounter requests CollisionQueries `query_attack`",
          "In the frozen command/entity order, revalidate provisional actions against the post-movement world, then resolve a newly committed attack's geometry, targets and random outcome once. Existing windups use their committed geometry contract. Capture the results in AttackLedger; Presentation cannot rerun these queries."
        ],
        [
          "P5: outcome application",
          "Encounter",
          "Apply the staged immediate outcomes once in the declared order, including contact consequences and attacks. Revalidate target eligibility against already applied outcomes without rerolling or changing committed geometry. Determine encounter/reward result values; no direct RunState/ProfileState mutation occurs here."
        ],
        [
          "P6: commit and publish",
          "Encounter publishes for `read_committed_results`",
          "Commit the complete tick, increment tick position once and publish detached snapshots plus identified committed results. Release the phase guard. Session may subsequently read results and route explicit run/profile transitions; Presentation displays the published data. Neither reader adds another tick."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "four-separate-operations",
      "status": "pass",
      "detail": [
        [
          "O1: release held physical input",
          "InputAdapter `clear_physical_input`, requested by Session",
          "Clear held state, previous-edge state and pending physical edges; advance the input-context generation. Consume the pause/resume/capture UI action as UI input. Re-arm each gameplay control only after observing it neutral in the new context, so a still-held key/button cannot reappear as a fresh press. This produces no gameplay release edge and cannot cancel Encounter preparation by itself."
        ],
        [
          "O2: cancel prepared actions",
          "Encounter `cancel_prepared`, requested by Session",
          "At a serialized control boundary, discard old-generation queued gameplay requests and clear uncommitted prepared actions. Return only after the cancellation is applied; if a tick is in flight, latch and finish the drain before another tick or resume. No cooldown/time increment, damage, new random draw or cast occurs. Existing committed windups/outcomes retain their contract."
        ],
        [
          "O3: solo pause",
          "Session `request_pause`",
          "After O1 and O2 for focus/modal/user-menu entry, hold the prior lifecycle state and set the engine solo pause state. Pause itself only stops future C-TICK admission and gameplay physics. It does not implicitly perform O1 or O2; direct internal pause must not be presented as the complete safe-menu sequence."
        ],
        [
          "O4: resume",
          "Session `resume`",
          "Require a valid active encounter, no held critical/save error, applied O2 where required, valid input path/capture and resolved modal focus. Perform O1 again to consume the resume/capture action and require neutral re-arm; restore the prior eligible playing/intermission state and unpause last. Resume alone does not tick, release or synthesize a cast. The next eligible C-TICK is the first gameplay advance."
        ]
      ]
    },
